          <Pad Id="ORoPcaf4d3LPzpdjJ2f0iV" Bounds="85,850,840,179" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Looks like a Qt window: gamma-space blending with premultiplied alpha, half-transparent parts included.&#xD;&#xA;- Draw it after the 3D scene (RenderEntity, Render Stage AfterScene) on the window or on a typeless 8-bit render texture: only there the layer can blend like a Qt window.&#xD;&#xA;- Other targets (e.g. a float or an SRgb render texture) blend in linear light like QtTexture, the colors then differ from a Qt window. Error shows a hint in that case.&#xD;&#xA;- No texture output: use QtTexture [Qt] where the patch needs the texture.&#xD;&#xA;- Size comes from the viewport. Space: only DIPTopLeft is implemented, other values behave like it.&#xD;&#xA;- Windows only (Direct3D 11). QtRenderer is Experimental: pins and behavior may still change.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
